{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DRIFT BLOCKER found during rebar-implement (green-on-origin-main AC). Plan hard-codes 53 C901 findings @ Ruff 0.15.19 (commit 0f5dbc88b). CURRENT origin/main 1767d9e401: pinned Ruff is 0.16.1 and 'ruff check --select C901 --config lint.mccabe.max-complexity=15 --statistics src/rebar' reports 69 findings (raw exit 1; JSON len 69; max 'validate_scorer' 16>15). ~8 ACs and the Baseline JSON Contract hard-code 'exactly 53' (baseline entries / active=53 / JSON findings), which is now unsatisfiable AND contradicts the green-on-origin-main AC that requires the baseline reflect the CURRENT census. The plan's own step 7 says treat baseline numbers as dated observations, not the gate contract. Reconciliation needed BEFORE implementation: replace the dated 53 with the current census (69) and make the count assertions parametric (assert against the live census, not a literal), then re-review (this edit will stale the current attestation). Not proceeding with implementation until reconciled."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785953378299308001,"uuid":"081d7e63-0b91-46a8-86ec-5cb97a6c42b7"}